{"question_id":"IOxV1RGZRT1LCL5U","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline","year":2016,"subject":"physics","chapter":"units-and-measurements","chapterGroup":"mechanics","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"content":"There are two Vernier calipers both of which have 1 cm divided into 10 equal divisions on the main scale.\nThe Vernier scale of one of the calipers (C<sub>1</sub>) has 10 equal divisions that correspond to 9 main scale\ndivisions. The Vernier scale of the other caliper (C<sub>2</sub>) has 10 equal divisions that correspond to 11 main\nscale divisions. The readings of the two calipers are shown in the figure. The measured values (in cm) by\ncalipers C<sub>1</sub> and C<sub>2</sub> respectively, are\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kwzykatk/1bdc3a94-7bc2-47f1-bebf-19d81b63c931/5a1ad480-597b-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzykatl.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kwzykatk/1bdc3a94-7bc2-47f1-bebf-19d81b63c931/5a1ad480-597b-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzykatl.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 70vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Units &amp; Measurements Question 46 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kwzykatk/1bdc3a94-7bc2-47f1-bebf-19d81b63c931/5a1ad480-597b-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzykatl.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kwzykatk/1bdc3a94-7bc2-47f1-bebf-19d81b63c931/5a1ad480-597b-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzykatl.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kwzykatk/1bdc3a94-7bc2-47f1-bebf-19d81b63c931/5a1ad480-597b-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzykatl.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kwzykatk/1bdc3a94-7bc2-47f1-bebf-19d81b63c931/5a1ad480-597b-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzykatl.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kwzykatk/1bdc3a94-7bc2-47f1-bebf-19d81b63c931/5a1ad480-597b-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzykatl.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kwzykatk/1bdc3a94-7bc2-47f1-bebf-19d81b63c931/5a1ad480-597b-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzykatl.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"2.85 and 2.82"},{"identifier":"B","content":"2.87 and 2.83"},{"identifier":"C","content":"2.87 and 2.86"},{"identifier":"D","content":"2.87 and 2.87"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"In both calipers C<sub>1</sub> and C<sub>2</sub>, 1 cm is divided into 10 equal divisions on the main scale. Thus, 1 division on the main scale is equal to x<sub>m1</sub> = x<sub>m2</sub> = 1 cm/10 = 0.1 cm. <br><br>In calipers C<sub>1</sub>, 10 equal divisions on the Vernier scale are equal to 9 main scale divisions.<br> Thus, 1 division on the Vernier scale of C<sub>1</sub> is equal to x<sub>v1</sub> = 9x<sub>m1</sub>/10 = 0.09 cm.<br><br> In calipers C<sub>2</sub>, 10 equal divisions on the Vernier scale are equal to 11 main scale divisions.<br> Thus, 1 division on the Vernier scale of C<sub>2</sub> is equal to x<sub>v2</sub> = 11x<sub>m2</sub>/10 = 0.11 cm.<br><br> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kwzyvyci/fd6742ae-c022-4775-8ee5-0c7b948e9ffd/9e2def30-597c-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzyvycj.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kwzyvyci/fd6742ae-c022-4775-8ee5-0c7b948e9ffd/9e2def30-597c-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzyvycj.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Units &amp; Measurements Question 46 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kwzyvyci/fd6742ae-c022-4775-8ee5-0c7b948e9ffd/9e2def30-597c-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzyvycj.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kwzyvyci/fd6742ae-c022-4775-8ee5-0c7b948e9ffd/9e2def30-597c-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzyvycj.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kwzyvyci/fd6742ae-c022-4775-8ee5-0c7b948e9ffd/9e2def30-597c-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzyvycj.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kwzyvyci/fd6742ae-c022-4775-8ee5-0c7b948e9ffd/9e2def30-597c-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzyvycj.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kwzyvyci/fd6742ae-c022-4775-8ee5-0c7b948e9ffd/9e2def30-597c-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzyvycj.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kwzyvyci/fd6742ae-c022-4775-8ee5-0c7b948e9ffd/9e2def30-597c-11ec-996b-3f9609fade5c/file-1kwzyvycj.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> <br>Let main scale reading be MSR and v<sup>th</sup> division of the Vernier scale coincides with m<sup>th</sup> division of the main scale (m is counted beyond MSR). The value measured by this calipers is<br><br>X = MSR + x = MSR + mx<sub>m</sub> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> vx<sub>v</sub> .........(1)<br><br>In calipers C<sub>1</sub>, MSR<sub>1</sub> = 2.8 cm, m<sub>1</sub> = 7 and v<sub>1</sub> = 7 and in calipers C<sub>2</sub>, MSR<sub>2</sub> = 2.8 cm, m<sub>2</sub> = 8 and v<sub>2</sub> = 7. Substitute these values in equation (1) to get<br><br